      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per offline discussion with Vadim, line 277~281 are justified.\n\nHowever, line 283~285 are still questioned.\n\nIn practice, it (should) never happen to have both CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC_TX and CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC_BITBANG set. However, if I should put them back to the original location (above line 259), then the code syntax can be seen as if it is possible to have both of them set. Otherwise, this code should be like this:\n\nif (ec_comm_is_uart_in_packet_mode(UART_EC) \u0026\u0026 !(flags_want \u0026 CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC_BITBANG))\n\tflags_want |\u003d (CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC | CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC_TX);\n\n, which makes bitbang mode checked twice in total. Just wanted to double check your comment before I update.",
